{
  "$comment": "The one set of source file endpoint fixtures (#87). Both toolchains read this file: agent/internal/httpapi/sources_fixtures_test.go and packages/schema/src/source-fixtures.test.ts. Never copy it per language. files are SourceFile answers (GET /api/pipelines/source), requests are SourceWriteRequest bodies (PUT), written are SourceWritten answers (PUT), errors are SourceError answers; each side checks them against the authoritative JSON Schema and against what it was generated into. The pairings the schema states in words (exactly one of expectedSha256 and expectedAbsent, reason exactly when rootUnavailable, sha256 only when changed) are held by both tests: a valid fixture keeps them, and the cases in pairingViolations pass the schema and break one.",
  "files": {
    "valid": [
      {
        "name": "in-a-directory",
        "why": "A file under src/ of a pipeline in a directory of its root, with CRLF line endings kept as they are.",
        "body": {
          "root": "/home/user/code",
          "directory": "orders",
          "path": "src/main.py",
          "text": "def run(message):\r\n    return message\r\n",
          "sha256": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
          "generated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "root-pipeline-generated",
        "why": "A root that is itself the pipeline has no directory; a file under generated/ says so.",
        "body": {
          "root": "/home/user/orders",
          "path": "generated/kpv-manifest.json",
          "text": "{}",
          "sha256": "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
          "generated": true
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "empty",
        "why": "An empty file is text.",
        "body": {
          "root": "/home/user/code",
          "directory": "orders",
          "path": "README",
          "text": "",
          "sha256": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
          "generated": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "invalid": [
